[RKL-1130] Prevent AbstractType::__destruct() from clearing static attribute caches.
PHP garbage collector may invoke the destructor of a leftover instance in the middle
of another import run, wiping self::$attributeCodeToId and self::$commonAttributesCache
while other instances still rely on them. Subsequent option writes then autovivify
partial cache entries without the apply_to key, causing
"Undefined array key 'apply_to'" warnings in _addAttributeParams().
See https://github.com/magento/magento2/issues/39585 (confirmed by Magento, P4).

diff --git a/Model/Import/Product/Type/AbstractType.php b/Model/Import/Product/Type/AbstractType.php
--- a/Model/Import/Product/Type/AbstractType.php
+++ b/Model/Import/Product/Type/AbstractType.php
@@ -720,7 +720,10 @@
      */
     public function __destruct()
     {
-        self::$attributeCodeToId = [];
-        self::$commonAttributesCache = [];
+        // BEGIN PATCH [RKL-1130] magento/magento2#39585
+        // GC may run this destructor mid-import and wipe caches still in use.
+        // self::$attributeCodeToId = [];
+        // self::$commonAttributesCache = [];
+        // END PATCH
     }
 }